  "review": [
    "The call is after both real original/JNI ChapterPackages have been cached, metadata reopened, and the TCP peer stopped. The product OnlineBookContentProvider delegates only to OnlineChapterContentService(.cacheOnly); both payload texts and source hrefs are checked against the same real chapters.",
    "The actual product HTML AST/Node builder and UniversalBookResourceAdapter feed the real CoreTextScrollEngine. Awaited start loads both chapters, awaits each document task and detached slice, then synchronously warms the chunks. The helper does not invoke unstructured ahead/behind/viewport warming.",
    "The test requires a legacy CoreText chunk and nonnil CTFrame, full UTF16 coverage of the JNI first&page body span by CTRuns and nonzero glyphs. The reader-content anchor attribute, chapter offset/reading-position roundtrip and both laid-out chapter texts are required.",
    "The real CoreTextChunkDrawView paints once into a UIKit renderer; a crop restricted to the actual body-line range must differ from the identically sized white crop. This excludes a title-only or placeholder-only success. It is offscreen product painting, not a ReaderView presentation assertion.",
    "The private helper is MainActor, matching product engine/UI/CTFrame ownership. The provider uses the existing nonisolated async cache path. Work is bounded to the two tiny fixture chapters, with the original 180-second method budget and cleanup retained.",
    "Whole-file reverse composition proves every old method/helper, request assertion, owned cache cleanup, original cold receipts, 17 method identities and all other code are unchanged. No new selector, host, route, VM, Store, or production source is introduced."
  ],
